  "description": "NARXAI crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C116 H96 Dy4 N12 O16,C2 H3 N1,0.5(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.539-3.843 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.17-111.36°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C118.5H99ClDy4N13O16. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
